  "summary": "Reproduced on base 4d0b9cd542 exactly as the card states, then fixed per triage direction 5916734614. The kernel:ready sync and the metadata:reloaded re-sync now resolve the protocol's flow view through the boot pull's own precedence decision (resolveFlowPrecedence with the engine's loader's-set reader, one private helper resolveFlowContenders shared by all three steps). Within a name the loader's set holds, the loader's entry now ranks before a stored row (ADR-0126 §2, Regime C). The metadata protocol hydrates a stored flow row without the artifact's protection envelope, and its flattened flow view (both faces) serves a shipped flow name from the loader's entries alone, so the stored row is reported by the boot pull as its own runtime-authored contender and never armed. Over two cold boots of the showcase composition on a database file, the loader's body is armed and executed, the receipt agrees with it, the control name is unchanged and an organization-scoped row stays out of reach. Two deviations need the seat's confirmation (see deviations and open_questions): the precedence rank flip inside a held name, and a one-clause correction of the pending 20864 changeset that this change makes false.",
  "tests": "At HEAD 22d8d3593e unless noted. (1) pnpm --filter @objectstack/service-automation exec vitest run: 160 files / 2002 tests passed (full run at 97bd52e852; since then one test title changed; the six precedence and sync files re-run at 22d8d3593e: 6 files / 43 passed). (2) pnpm --filter @objectstack/metadata-protocol exec vitest run: 194 passed / 3 skipped files, 2879 passed / 19 skipped tests (protocol.ts unchanged since; the new file and protocol.tenant-authored-write re-run at 22d8d3593e: 21 passed). (3) pnpm --filter @objectstack/metadata-protocol --filter @objectstack/service-automation --filter @objectstack/dogfood run typecheck: clean; service-automation typecheck re-run at 22d8d3593e, check:test-typecheck OK 0 errors. (4) dogfood, isolated project, after rebuilding both packages: flow-shipped-name-stored-row-boot (new, 6 cases) + flow-provenance-server-held + automation-authoring-doors-durable + packaged-flow-write-door-parity: 4 files / 31 passed. On the base the new file was red 3 of 6: armed body was the stored one, the triggered run executed the stored body's node, the receipt rendered both contenders as the package. (5) pnpm lint (eslint . --no-inline-config, whole repo): exit 0 at 22d8d3593e, 209s. Ablations, fix committed first, every leg through scripts/ablation-replace.mjs (anchor x1 -> x0, blob changed; restore proven blob == HEAD and git diff HEAD empty): unit legs, subjects imported from src: A1 kernel:ready sync precedence removed -> 3 red of 32; A2 metadata:reloaded re-sync precedence removed -> 2 red of 32; A3 rank put back runtime-first -> 10 red of 32; A4 hydration graft put back for flow -> 2 red of 9; A5 stored-row half of the view filter removed -> 4 red of 9; A6 registry half of the view filter removed -> 1 red of 9. Dogfood legs (dist-resolved): D1 metadata-protocol view stored-row half removed -> rebuild (the declaration step exited 1 on the now-unused binding; JS bundles emitted), ablation-dist-preflight marker present in 2 built files -> 2 red of 6 (arming, execution), receipt green; restore rebuild exit 0, preflight --absent 0 of 24 files, tree clean. D2 service-automation rank put back runtime-first -> rebuild exit 0, preflight present in 2 built files (source spelling via --source-marker) -> 1 red of 6 (the receipt-agrees pin: the boot pull recorded the stored row armed while the sync armed the loader's body); restore rebuild exit 0, preflight --absent 0 of 6 files, tree clean.",
