  "open_questions": [
    {
      "question": "Confirm the precedence rank flip inside a held name. The claim scoped flow-precedence.ts to exposing the existing decision without re-shaping it. Measured: the base decision arms the loader's body only because the hydration grafted the package's provenance onto the stored row (both contenders ranked package, arrival order decided). With the stored row reported with its own provenance, which the direction's second bullet requires, the base rank (runtime before package, the ADR-0005 direction #11997 wrote and #20864 pinned as 'the tenant row armed') arms the stored row, the opposite of the direction's first bullet.",
      "options": [
        "A — keep the flip: within a name the loader's set holds, package ranks before runtime (ADR-0126 §2 Regime C, ADR-0131 D6). Business need: the measured case, a sealed managed flow overridden on every cold boot; no real deployment relies on a stored row winning a shipped name, since every authoring door refuses that write as a locked base. Long-term: one rule, stated by the accepted ADR, in the one precedence function every step calls, with an ADR anchor. AI-error prevention: a stored row can no longer silently replace a sealed definition, and the receipt names it for what it is. Startup scope: no new surface, no new gate; the only moved behaviour is the held-name-with-stored-row case.",
        "B — revert the flip and keep the hydration graft: the boot pull keeps arming the loader's body by arrival order, the receipt keeps rendering both contenders as the package (the card's own complaint), and the direction's second bullet is not delivered. Business need: none served. Long-term: correctness by accident of registry order. AI-error prevention: the receipt stays unable to tell the two apart. Startup scope: smaller diff, larger residual.",
        "C — hold the PR for a maintainer ruling on whether the ADR-0005 direction still binds flows. Costs a round trip on a p1 security card; ADR-0126 §2 already answers it for Regime C."
      ],
      "recommendation": "A, because on all four axes it is the only option that delivers both bullets of the direction: the business case is exactly the measured one, ADR-0126 §2 already decides the rule, it closes the silent-override path structurally rather than by arrival order, and it adds no surface or gate."
    },
    {
      "question": "Confirm the correction of the pending release note .changeset/20864-precedence-loader-set.md: one clause removed ('a flow authored in the deployment wins over the packaged flow of that name (ADR-0005)'). This PR makes it false and it has not shipped. check-empty-changeset stays red by design for a deliberate correction of somebody else's pending note.",
      "options": [
        "A — keep the correction in this PR. Business need: the release notes an upgrading operator reads stay true. Long-term: one release, one consistent statement of the rule. AI-error prevention: an agent grepping the CHANGELOG is not told the retired direction. Startup scope: one-line edit, no gate change.",
        "B — restore the note from the base and let this PR's own changeset state the new rule. The same release would then ship two contradicting sentences; an agent reading the older one is told the opposite of the runtime."
      ],
      "recommendation": "A, because it keeps the published CHANGELOG true at zero cost on every axis; the red gate is the intended human confirmation path, not a defect."
    }
  ],
  "out_of_scope_findings": [
    "class: b · reach: GET /api/v1/meta/flow/NAME answers 200 serving a stored row's body under the shipping package's provenance, for a flow name a managed package ships (measured on the showcase composition, database file, cold boot, on base 4d0b9cd542 and at 22d8d3593e); after this PR it also disagrees with GET /api/v1/meta/flow, which serves the loader's body · evidence: contract ADR-0126 §2 'Never silent override, never an overlay read path' and ruling 5904938166 rule 1 (a body's package-provenance stamps are display only); Seam: spec:ADR-0126 §2 Regime C (flow) → runtime:metadata-protocol getMetaItem (env-wide stored-row lookup, then the artifact envelope grafted over it) · family: #15206 (what happens to hatch-written rows: keep, refuse, migrate) — fold into it, no single-point card · dedupe words: 'meta flow by-name stored row shipped name' · 'getMetaItem flow overlay package provenance' · 'shipped flow list by-name disagree' · 'hatch row served as the package'",
    "carrier: 承接者:无 · noted, not filed — the objectql registry's Collision warning on hydrating a stored row over a shipped name says every read serves the stored row; for a flow only the by-name door still does (packages/objectql/src/registry.ts). Runtime log wording, no defect class.",
    "carrier: 承接者:无 · noted, not filed — the CLI startup banner cites ADR-0005 overlay precedence for every shadowed flow (packages/cli/src/utils/format.ts); the armed and shadowed facts it prints come from the receipt and are correct.",
    "carrier: the next PR touching FlowContender (routing from the #20864 review) · noted, not filed — the FlowContender and FlowShadowingRecord docblocks in service-automation engine.ts still describe the ADR-0005 direction.",
    "carrier: 承接者:无 · noted, not filed — the metadata_org_scoped_unhydrated boot warning says a listed flow 'will NOT bind its triggers'; for a shipped name that is true of the organization-scoped row only, the loader's flow stays bound (measured in the new dogfood pin)."
  ],
  "gates": "node scripts/pm/dispatch-gates.mjs --repo objectstack-ai/objectstack --commands at 22d8d3593e (merge base 4d0b9cd542; origin/main aaad682dbc, 3 commits none touching this change's inputs) derived 77 families; --ran with exit codes recorded: 77 derived, 77 run, 0 NOT-MEASURED. 76 exit 0; node scripts/check-empty-changeset.mjs --base origin/main exit 1 (deliberate correction of the pending 20864 note, red by design, confirmation asked on the PR); pnpm check:dual-build-cjs-loads first exit 3 PREREQUISITE NOT MET (8 unrelated packages had no dist/), exit 0 after building them. Beyond the derivation: pnpm lint exit 0 (whole repo). CI convergence: in_progress, not awaited.",
